Three things in those traces are worth reading.

The first question needed both tools, and it used each for what it is for: the
exact figure from the warehouse, the explanation from the documents. That split
is the whole of Parts III and IV in one answer.

The second was asked to 'compute' a percentage, and it did not compute anything.
It recognised that margin_pct is already a defined metric and asked the
warehouse for it — so the number came from Chapter 15's semantic layer rather
than from arithmetic over two figures the model had to keep straight. The best
tool call is often the one that makes a second call unnecessary.

The third has no answer anywhere in the corpus. It searched twice, found the
depot mentioned in three documents, and refused — naming what it did find so a
person can judge whether to look elsewhere.
